cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TEFAR in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "TEFAR: TMS-EEG / EEG FieldTrip Artefact Removal"
abstract: >-
  A lightweight, configurable MATLAB framework for automated
  artefact-component classification in EEG and TMS-EEG, built on
  FieldTrip. A shared scoring engine detects line noise, blinks,
  lateral eye movements, cranial muscle, cardiac activity, and the
  TMS decay and recharge transients from established independent-
  component signatures, using robust (median/MAD) thresholds, and
  suggests components for removal subject to expert confirmation.
